8:09:17Z","body":"There was no `HasConnections` in 4.3, it was added in 4.4 (203d3be200). \n\nDisregarding that, `GodotObject.GetSignalConnectionList` was already available in 4.3, and it did return the same internal `EventSignalMiddleman` as it does to this day in 4.7.\n \n<img width=\"1206\" height=\"304\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/91115ef0-ffac-47db-81fe-55ffb83e2513\" />\n\nSo this is not a regression from 4.3, the internal connection has been there since C# signals were implemented as events. The underlying issue (engine-internal C# signal plumbing being visible to script callers) is still valid.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5270772956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]